.TH DIGAARD 1 "2026" "digaard 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
digaard \- a modern DNS query CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B digaard
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fINAME\fR...
.br
.B digaard
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fB-f\fR \fIFILE\fR
.br
.B digaard
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fB-x\fR \fIIP\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B digaard
is a dig-style command-line DNS client with modern transport support (Do53,
DoT, DoH, DoQ), full EDNS(0), DNSSEC record display + AD-based validation,
IDN input, batch mode with bounded concurrency, JSON output, and latency
statistics.

It is a pure client — no caching, no resolver logic, one query in, one
response out.

.SH POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I NAME
One or more domain names. IDN input is punycode-encoded before wire send.
Ignored when \fB-x\fR interprets the argument as an IP address.

.SH QUERY SHAPE
.TP
\fB-t\fR, \fB--type\fR=\fITYPE\fR
Record type: \fBA\fR (default), \fBAAAA\fR, \fBMX\fR, \fBTXT\fR, \fBCNAME\fR,
\fBNS\fR, \fBSOA\fR, \fBPTR\fR, \fBSRV\fR, \fBCAA\fR, \fBHTTPS\fR, \fBSVCB\fR,
\fBDNSKEY\fR, \fBDS\fR, \fBRRSIG\fR, \fBNSEC3\fR, \fBANY\fR, ....
.TP
\fB-c\fR, \fB--class\fR=\fICLASS\fR
DNS class: \fBIN\fR (default), \fBCH\fR, \fBHS\fR, \fBANY\fR.
.TP
\fB-x\fR, \fB--reverse\fR
Interpret positional arguments as IPv4/IPv6 addresses and synthesise the
corresponding PTR query.
.TP
\fB--aa\fR, \fB--ad\fR, \fB--cd\fR
Set the AA / AD / CD header bits.
.TP
\fB--no-rd\fR
Clear the Recursion Desired bit (default: set).
.TP
\fB--dnssec\fR
Set the EDNS DO (DNSSEC OK) bit.

.SH TRANSPORT
.TP
\fB-s\fR, \fB--server\fR=\fISERVER\fR
Nameserver address (IP or hostname). Repeatable. Bare
\fB@\fR\fIserver\fR is also accepted anywhere in argv.
.TP
\fB--server-strategy\fR=\fIMODE\fR
When multiple \fB-s\fR are given: \fBfirst\fR (default), \fBrace\fR, or
\fBround-robin\fR.
.TP
\fB-p\fR, \fB--port\fR=\fIPORT\fR
Override the default port for the chosen transport.
.TP
\fB--udp\fR, \fB--tcp\fR, \fB--tls\fR, \fB--https\fR, \fB--quic\fR
Force transport. Default \fB--udp\fR.
.TP
\fB-4\fR / \fB-6\fR
Bind outbound socket IPv4-only / IPv6-only.
.TP
\fB--timeout\fR=\fIMS\fR
Per-query timeout in milliseconds (default 5000).
.TP
\fB--retry\fR=\fIN\fR
Retries on UDP timeout (default 2; UDP only).
.TP
\fB--tls-servername\fR=\fINAME\fR
SNI / expected certificate name override. Defaults to the server host.
.TP
\fB--tls-insecure\fR
Skip TLS certificate verification. Debugging only.
.TP
\fB--tls-ca\fR=\fIFILE\fR
PEM file with additional trust roots. Repeatable.
.TP
\fB--doh-method\fR=\fIMETHOD\fR
DoH HTTP method: \fBPOST\fR (default) or \fBGET\fR.
.TP
\fB--doh-path\fR=\fIPATH\fR
DoH URL path (default \fB/dns-query\fR).

.SH EDNS(0)
.TP
\fB--edns\fR / \fB--no-edns\fR
Enable / disable OPT record.
.TP
\fB--edns-bufsize\fR=\fIBYTES\fR
Advertised UDP payload size (default 1232).
.TP
\fB--subnet\fR=\fIPREFIX\fR
EDNS Client Subnet (RFC 7871), e.g. \fI192.0.2.0/24\fR.
.TP
\fB--nsid\fR
Request NSID (RFC 5001).
.TP
\fB--cookie\fR
Send DNS Cookie (RFC 7873) with 8 random bytes.
.TP
\fB--cookie-hex\fR=\fIHEX\fR
Send DNS Cookie with an explicit hex value.
.TP
\fB--pad\fR
Enable EDNS Padding (RFC 7830), rounding wire size to a 128-byte block.
.TP
\fB--pad-size\fR=\fISIZE\fR
Custom padding block size in bytes.
.TP
\fB--edge\fR
Decode Extended DNS Errors (RFC 8914) in the ADDITIONAL section.

.SH DNSSEC
.TP
\fB--validate\fR
Classify response as SECURE, INSECURE, or BOGUS. Implies \fB--dnssec\fR.
.TP
\fB--trust-anchor\fR=\fIFILE\fR
BIND-style trust-anchor file with DNSKEY records. Repeatable.

.SH BATCH / SCRIPTING
.TP
\fB-f\fR, \fB--file\fR=\fIPATH\fR
Read domains from a file, one per line. Use \fB-\fR for stdin. Blank lines
and lines starting with \fB#\fR are ignored.
.TP
\fB-j\fR, \fB--concurrency\fR=\fIN\fR
Max concurrent in-flight queries. Default: min(cpus, 32).
.TP
\fB--stats\fR
Print per-response query time on stdout AND an end-of-run summary
(min/avg/p50/p95/max/error rate) on stderr.

.SH OUTPUT
.TP
\fB--text\fR
Dig-style text (default).
.TP
\fB--json\fR
NDJSON — one JSON object per response.
.TP
\fB-q\fR, \fB--short\fR
Only RDATA, one per line (like \fBdig +short\fR).
.TP
\fB--color\fR=\fIWHEN\fR
\fBauto\fR (default), \fBalways\fR, \fBnever\fR.
.TP
\fB--hex\fR
Print raw response wire bytes as an xxd-style dump.

.SH META
.TP
\fB-v\fR, \fB--verbose\fR
Increase log verbosity. Repeatable: \fB-v\fR info, \fB-vv\fR debug, \fB-vvv\fR trace.
.TP
\fB--config\fR=\fIFILE\fR
TOML config file. See \fBCONFIG FILE\fR below.
.TP
\fB-h\fR, \fB--help\fR
Print help and exit.
.TP
\fB-V\fR, \fB--version\fR
Print version and exit.

.SH DIG-STYLE SHORTCUTS
Rewritten before parsing:
.PP
.RS 4
\fB+short\fR   → \fB--short\fR
.br
\fB+dnssec\fR  → \fB--dnssec\fR
.br
\fB+tcp\fR     → \fB--tcp\fR
.br
\fB+nord\fR    → \fB--no-rd\fR
.br
\fB+adflag\fR  → \fB--ad\fR
.br
\fB+cdflag\fR  → \fB--cd\fR
.RE

.SH CONFIG FILE
Path resolution: \fB--config\fR > \fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/digaard/config.toml\fR >
\fB~/.config/digaard/config.toml\fR. Missing files are ignored unless
\fB--config\fR was explicit.

.PP
.EX
default_server    = "https://dns.quad9.net/dns-query"
default_transport = "https"
default_format    = "pretty"
color             = "auto"
timeout_ms        = 3000
retry             = 2
concurrency       = 16
.EE

CLI flags always override config values.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
All queries succeeded.
.TP
\fB1\fR
One or more queries failed at runtime.
.TP
\fB2\fR
Argument parsing failed.

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.EX
digaard example.com @1.1.1.1
digaard -t MX gmail.com @1.1.1.1 --stats
digaard example.com --https @cloudflare-dns.com --doh-method GET
digaard --tls example.com @dns.google
digaard -x 8.8.8.8
digaard -s 1.1.1.1 -s 9.9.9.9 --server-strategy race example.com
cat domains.txt | digaard -f - --json -j 32
digaard cloudflare.com --validate --https @cloudflare-dns.com
digaard example.com +short +dnssec
.EE

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dig (1),
.BR host (1),
.BR delv (1).

